  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(ABCD\\) be a parallelogram with \\(\\angle ABC=120^\\circ,\\) \\(AB=16,\\) and \\(BC=10.\\) Extend \\(\\overline{CD}\\) through \\(D\\) to \\(E\\) so that \\(DE=4.\\) If \\(\\overline{BE}\\) intersects \\(\\overline{AD}\\) at \\(F,\\) then \\(FD\\) is closest to",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(5\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
