    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1990-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because \\(AB\\parallel ED,\\) triangles \\(ABF\\) and \\(DEF\\) are similar. Hence \\[ \\frac{AF}{FD}=\\frac{AB}{DE}=\\frac{16}{4}=4. \\] Since \\(AF+FD=AD=BC=10,\\) we get \\(5FD=10,\\) so \\(FD=2.\\)\n\nThus the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Use that \\(\\overline{AB}\\parallel\\overline{ED}\\)",
        "Triangles \\(ABF\\) and \\(DEF\\) are similar"
      ],
